# LeakSanitizer suppressions for intentional, process-lifetime allocations.
# litestl's own leak tracker (alloc::print_blocks via test_end) remains the
# real leak check for library allocations.

# Per-thread tracker list, deliberately never freed (util/alloc.cc getMemList).
leak:getMemList

# Binding descriptors are allocated with `new` and intentionally never freed
# (scaffolding for a future constexpr redesign; see CLAUDE.md "Binding system").
leak:litestl::binding::
leak:defineBindings
# test_binding_iface builds a descriptor with `new` in the test itself, so its
# stacks start outside litestl::binding::.
leak:test_adaptor_methods
